    <description>Fires when AF_RequisitionStatus__c changes to Approved. Generates the Internal Requisition Form and confirms approval to the Opportunity Owner. 2026-09-17: Create_Requisition_Document switched from the generic AF_DocumentGenerationService (plain-text .txt, single-record formula body only) to AF_InternalRequisitionFormService, a dedicated Apex invocable that renders a styled PDF via AF_PdfGenerationService (Blob.toPdf()) - same branded look as AF_FL_AppraisalItem_GenerateBookInSheet&apos;s Eval Expert Book-In Sheet - and lists every flagged accessory/PDI OpportunityLineItem with its job specification, which a Flow-only formula body could not do (no Flow in this org loops line items into a string; the Sales Order document delegates to Apex for the same reason). The old AF_Formula_DocumentTitle/FileName/DocumentBody formulas were removed as dead code since the new Apex action takes only opportunityId and builds title/filename/body itself. Distribution to After Sales is intentionally manual, not automated: per LFRDN-346 business decision (2026-09-16), there is no After Sales persona/queue in Salesforce, so the Sales Rep uses the native Send Email action on the Opportunity - attaching the generated IRF file and selecting the AF_ET_Opp_RequisitionForAfterSales template - to distribute it themselves. An earlier version of this flow auto-emailed a configurable AF_ProcessEmailRouting__mdt.AfterSalesTeam address; that branch (Send_AfterSales_Email / Decide_AfterSales_Email_Configured / Get_AfterSales_Routing) was removed 2026-09-16 for this reason. 2026-09-09: Owner Confirmation email upgraded from plain text to branded HTML (sendRichBody=true). Tried real EmailTemplate (AF_ET_Opp_RequisitionApproved) + AF_SendTemplateEmailAction (Apex wrapper around Messaging.sendEmail(templateId=...)) first, since Flow&apos;s own &quot;emailTemplate&quot; core action is confirmed NOT a valid InvocableActionType in this org&apos;s Metadata API - but Messaging.sendEmail to a User target hard-requires saveAsActivity=false, and with that forced false, ZERO EmailMessage row is created (confirmed empirically: isSuccess()=true, no EmailMessage ever appears), unlike emailSimple+logEmailOnSend which reliably logs even to User recipients. Reverted to emailSimple/inline-HTML for this reason.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_OwnerConfirmationBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;margin:0;padding:16px;background-color:#F4F4F6;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #E2E5EA;border-top:4px solid #1E7A46;padding:20px 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;display:inline-block;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:3px;background-color:#DFF3E6;color:#1E7A46;font-size:11px;font-weight:bold;letter-spacing:0.5px;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:12px;&quot;&gt;Approved&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;color:#0B2545;&quot;&gt;Internal Requisition Form Approved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;Your Internal Requisition Form request for &lt;strong&gt;&apos; &amp; {!$Record.Name} &amp; &apos;&lt;/strong&gt; has been approved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;The form has been generated and attached to the Opportunity. Please use Send Email on the Opportunity to distribute it to the After Sales team using the Internal Requisition Form - After Sales template.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&apos;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>AF_Formula_OwnerConfirmationSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Approved: Internal Requisition Form for &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Your Internal Requisition Form request for &quot; &amp; {!$Record.Name} &amp; &quot; was approved.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
